WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:14.003
Not only did Meg look different at Annie's party, she acted differently, too.

2
00:00:14.004 --> 00:00:20.804
She walked with her shoulders pulled back proudly, coolly acknowledging people in an aloof manner as she passed them.

3
00:00:20.805 --> 00:00:27.134
When it came to dancing, Meg was selective, choosing only those partners who looked wealthy and handsome.

4
00:00:27.135 --> 00:00:35.511
She loved all the attention she was getting as she tossed her head back and laughed loudly (almost as loud as Jo) while dancing,

5
00:00:35.512 --> 00:00:40.428
quite aware that some of the other girls were jealously staring and whispering about her.

6
00:00:40.429 --> 00:00:46.895
"Oh, I need to rest my feet," Meg gasped to her dance partner, who happened to be Annie's older brother Ned.

7
00:00:46.896 --> 00:00:52.846
"Only if you promise to let me have the next dance," Ned said, leading her to some chairs.

8
00:00:52.847 --> 00:00:56.227
Touching his shoulder lightly, as she had seen Sallie do,

9
00:00:56.228 --> 00:01:02.528
Meg said in a flirty voice, "I'll think about it. Now be a pet and get me a drink."

10
00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:07.069
Ned happily obliged while Meg collapsed onto a chair next to Sallie.

11
00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:11.876
"Meg, you are the darling of the party tonight," Sallie giggled.

12
00:01:11.877 --> 00:01:16.814
Meg lightly touched her eyes with her handkerchief, being careful not to erase her make-up.

13
00:01:16.815 --> 00:01:20.599
"I have never had so much fun," she confessed.

14
00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:24.811
"Well, I think Ned really likes you," Sallie whispered.

15
00:01:24.812 --> 00:01:29.446
Meg looked over at Ned who was carrying two drinks over to where she sat.

16
00:01:29.447 --> 00:01:33.970
Ned was a tall, handsome young man, about two years older than Meg.

17
00:01:33.971 --> 00:01:40.419
She knew from Annie that their parents were hoping he would find a suitable wife and marry in the very near future.

18
00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:44.466
Meg hoped she might be that special someone he was looking for.

19
00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:48.250
"Here you go," Ned said. As he handed the glass to Meg.

20
00:01:48.251 --> 00:01:51.501
However, he accidentally spilled some of the drink.

21
00:01:51.502 --> 00:01:56.830
"My dress!" cried Meg, jumping up and trying to wipe off the mess with her handkerchief.

22
00:01:56.831 --> 00:02:00.567
"I'm such a clumsy baboon!" exclaimed Ned.

23
00:02:00.568 --> 00:02:08.969
"That's quite all right," reassured Meg, "I'll just step into the ladies' room and clean this off. Please excuse me."

24
00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:12.370
She left Ned standing there awkwardly with Sallie.

25
00:02:12.371 --> 00:02:16.364
At the Moffats, even the ladies' room was a lavish affair.

26
00:02:16.365 --> 00:02:21.909
Massive gold-trimmed mirrors covered one wall above a solid oak rectangular table.

27
00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:29.960
Gold-plated brushes and hand mirrors, embroidered handkerchiefs, and fresh red roses in crystal vases adorned the table.

28
00:02:29.961 --> 00:02:35.048
Meg sat on one of the dozen plush velvet chairs set out along the table.

29
00:02:35.049 --> 00:02:38.556
On the other side of the wall were the toilets and wash basins.

30
00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:44.929
Glancing at herself in the mirror and admiring her reflection, Meg proceeded to remove the stain on her dress.

31
00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.990
Luckily it came off and only needed to be dried.

32
00:02:47.991 --> 00:02:51.982
Meg pressed a handkerchief against the spot to soak up the moisture.

33
00:02:51.983 --> 00:02:55.662
Outside she could hear the faint sounds of a familiar tune.

34
00:02:55.663 --> 00:03:00.050
Humming along, she closed her eyes and imagined she was dancing with Ned.

35
00:03:00.051 --> 00:03:06.541
"Did you see how she flirted with Ned?" came a high-pitched voice loudly from the washroom area.

36
00:03:06.542 --> 00:03:09.034
The wall blocked Meg's view of the speaker.

37
00:03:09.035 --> 00:03:13.354
For some reason, however, Meg knew the speaker was referring to her.

38
00:03:13.355 --> 00:03:20.222
Then another girl spoke in a lower voice but still clear enough to hear, "That's Belle's dress she's wearing."

39
00:03:20.223 --> 00:03:24.550
"Of course it is. Her family can't afford anything like that.

40
00:03:24.551 --> 00:03:28.707
I heard she came tonight wearing a cotton summer dress."

41
00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:31.125
Cruel laughter followed that remark.

42
00:03:31.126 --> 00:03:36.481
"Does she think Ned Moffat will ask her out?" the high-pitched voice asked.

43
00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:42.351
"Heavens, no! Annie and she are friends, but they would never allow her to become family."

44
00:03:42.352 --> 00:03:51.825
Listening intently to their conversation, Meg did not realize that she had rolled her handkerchief into a tight ball and was clenching her jaw.

45
00:03:51.826 --> 00:04:00.509
Never had she been so humiliated. She lowered her shaking hands and slowly turned to look at the stranger staring back at her from the mirror.

46
00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:05.184
Until that moment, Meg did not realize how different she really looked.

47
00:04:05.185 --> 00:04:13.707
In fact, she was unrecognizable. "I hate you," she spat to her own pathetic face, which did not look so lovely any more.

48
00:04:13.708 --> 00:04:19.907
Fantasies of marrying Ned Moffat and being the mistress of their impressive estate vanished into thin air.

49
00:04:19.908 --> 00:04:25.220
Delusions of being wealthy and sophisticated like Annie and Sallie faded even more quickly.

50
00:04:25.221 --> 00:04:29.621
Suddenly Meg longed for the comfort and simplicity of her family and home.

51
00:04:29.622 --> 00:04:37.705
Glittering gold and sparkling crystal no longer appealed to her, nor did the lovely silk and lace dresses of spring colors.

52
00:04:37.706 --> 00:04:42.794
Meg just wanted to be herself and be with those who loved her for who she was.

53
00:04:42.795 --> 00:04:48.179
Blindly trying to find her way out of the Moffats' home, Meg was not looking where she was going.

54
00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:52.395
"Oh!" she exclaimed as she bumped into someone and fell to the floor.

55
00:04:52.396 --> 00:05:01.590
In her quest to locate the front entrance without attracting attention, Meg had run into someone heading toward the very festivities she was trying to escape.

56
00:05:01.591 --> 00:05:07.667
"I beg your pardon, Miss," the young man apologized profusely, extending a hand to help her up.

57
00:05:07.668 --> 00:05:12.449
"No, I should be the one apologizing, I wasn't looking . . . Laurie!"

58
00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:16.019
Meg shouted in relief when she saw who her victim was.

59
00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:21.504
Laurie stared at her for a long time, obviously not immediately recognizing her.

60
00:05:21.505 --> 00:05:27.200
When he finally did, his jaw dropped, and he looked at her critically with a disapproving eye.

61
00:05:27.201 --> 00:05:32.803
"Meg? Sweet, innocent Meg? That can't be you!" were his first words.

62
00:05:32.804 --> 00:05:38.488
"Laurie, I'm so happy to see you!" cried Meg. "I've been so miserable."

63
00:05:38.489 --> 00:05:42.430
Laurie, who was still in shock, demanded, "What happened to you?

64
00:05:42.431 --> 00:05:46.148
What's that on your face? You look like a stranger to me!"

65
00:05:46.149 --> 00:05:49.691
He was very upset and did not hide the fact.

66
00:05:49.692 --> 00:05:54.529
"Laurie," Meg pleaded, "please, I know I don't look like myself.

67
00:05:54.530 --> 00:06:03.198
I don't feel like myself either. But right now, I'm so miserable and I have to get out of here. Won't you please help me?"

68
00:06:03.199 --> 00:06:10.130
Softening as he heard the desperation in Meg's voice, Laurie wrapped his arms around her and comforted her, saying,

69
00:06:10.131 --> 00:06:14.280
"I'm sorry for being so rude, Meg, but I was quite shocked.

70
00:06:14.281 --> 00:06:17.990
Of course, I'll help you. Come, now, let's get you home."

71
00:06:17.991 --> 00:06:23.703
Like a true gentleman, Laurie, without another remark about her appearance, escorted Meg home.

72
00:06:23.704 --> 00:06:28.347
When Meg got home, she told her family what had happened.

73
00:06:28.348 --> 00:06:33.274
She spoke honestly about how she envied the wealth of her friends and their lifestyle.

74
00:06:33.275 --> 00:06:39.232
Then she told them about overhearing the conversation in the ladies' room that eventually opened her eyes to reality.

75
00:06:39.233 --> 00:06:45.769
"I realize that what I have now may be simple to some, but it's very dear to me," sniffed Meg.

76
00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:50.503
"I wouldn't change my life now with any amount of money or pretty things."

77
00:06:50.504 --> 00:06:53.208
"And we wouldn't want you any other way.

78
00:06:53.209 --> 00:06:57.378
You're our Meg and we love you," comforted Mother.

79
00:06:57.379 --> 00:07:04.152
Hugging her mother and sisters, Meg gratefully accepted the precious life she had.
